  "question": {
    "text": "A radar sends an electromagnetic signal of electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> which strikes a target on line of sight at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math> in a medium. After that, a part of signal (echo) reflects back towards the radar with same velocity and by same path. If the signal was transmitted at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;from radar, then after how much time echo will reach to the radar?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Mi41I",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
